-30", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 1.039, "filing_name": "Tesla Inc 10-Q Q2 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000095017022012936/tsla-20220630.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10Q_2022-03-31__legal_proceedings__0000", "ticker": "TSLA", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "legal_proceedings", "score": 1.3481, "filing_name": "Tesla Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000095017022006034/tsla-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10Q_2022-03-31__legal_proceedings__0001", "ticker": "TSLA", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "legal_proceedings", "score": 1.3429, "filing_name": "Tesla Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000095017022006034/tsla-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10Q_2022-03-31__financial_statements__0079", "ticker": "TSLA", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 1.0719, "filing_name": "Tesla Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000095017022006034/tsla-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 19, "dropped_candidates": 182, "token_estimate": 31987, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Tesla's FY2025 10-K (fiscal year ended December 31, 2025) points to Note 13 for its material pending legal proceedings [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000]. That note describes litigation over driver assistance technology (a consumer class action and securities class actions) and a product liability verdict, discrimination and harassment actions brought by the California CRD and the EEOC, and Delaware derivative suits [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0153][TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0155]. It also describes regular government information requests and a data-incident class action, and states that no agency in an ongoing investigation has concluded wrongdoing occurred [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0157]. Earlier filings also disclosed environmental matters under Item 103 of Regulation S-K, such as a waste segregation investigation that was settled in February 2024 [TSLA_10Q_2024-03-31__legal_proceedings__0000]. Tesla says it is unable to reasonably estimate the possible loss or range of loss unless noted [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0156].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "TSLA", "company": "Tesla Inc", "findings": [{"point": "In Benavides v. Tesla, a jury in the Southern District of Florida awarded $129 million in compensatory damages (Tesla 33% at fault) and $200 million in punitive damages over a 2019 Autopilot-related accident; Tesla filed a post-trial motion on September 15, 2025 and recorded an immaterial accrual (FY2025 10-K, fiscal year ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0155", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0156"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "A consumer class action over driver assistance technology had a limited class certified on August 18, 2025; the Ninth Circuit granted Tesla's petition to appeal on December 18, 2025, and a securities class action filed August 4, 2025 in the Western District of Texas alleges misrepresentations about Autopilot, FSD (Supervised) and Robotaxi (FY2025 10-K, fiscal year ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0153", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0155"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The California CRD's discrimination complaint has trial set for July 20, 2026, and the EEOC's civil complaint is in discovery with no trial date set (FY2025 10-K, fiscal year ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0152"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "In the directors' compensation derivative suit, the court approved the settlement on January 8, 2025 and awarded plaintiff's counsel fees of approximately $176 million, which Tesla appealed to the Delaware Supreme Court (FY2025 10-K, fiscal year ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0149"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Tesla regularly receives information requests and subpoenas from regulators such as NHTSA, the NTSB, the SEC and the DOJ, and a class action over a 2023 data misappropriation incident is also disclosed (FY2025 10-K, fiscal year ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0156", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0157"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": null, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000", "claim": "Item 3 refers to Note 13 for material pending legal proceedings", "quote": "see Note 13, Commitments and Contingencies, to the consolidated financial statements"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0153", "claim": "Consumer class action over driver assistance technology; limited class certified; Ninth Circuit granted petition", "quote": "on August 18, 2025, the Court certified a limited class comprised of California consumers"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0155", "claim": "Benavides verdict and Texas securities class action", "quote": "The jury awarded $129 million in total compensatory damages"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0156", "claim": "Post-trial motion, immaterial accrual, inability to estimate loss, regulator requests", "quote": "the Company has recorded an immaterial accrual"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0152", "claim": "CRD and EEOC discrimination and harassment proceedings", "quote": "The trial is currently set for July 20, 2026."}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0149", "claim": "Directors' compensation derivative suit settlement and fee award", "quote": "awarded Plaintiff's counsel fees in the amount of approximately $176 million"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0157", "claim": "No agency has concluded wrongdoing; data incident class action", "quote": "no government agency in any ongoing investigation has concluded that any wrongdoing occurred"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10Q_2024-03-31__legal_proceedings__0000", "claim": "Environmental waste segregation matter settled in February 2024", "quote": "payment of approximately $1.5 million in civil penalties and fees"}], "coverage": {"companies_used": [{"ticker": "TSLA", "forms": ["10-K", "10-Q"], "fiscal_periods": ["FY2025, ended December 31, 2025", "Q1 FY2024, ended March 31, 2024"]}], "companies_missing": [], "data_as_of": "10-K FY2025, period ended December 31, 2025, filed 2026-01-29"}, "gaps": ["The FY2025 10-K retrieved excerpts omit the opening of the Note 13 legal proceedings, including the full text on the 2018 CEO performance award litigation and the first part of the SEC-related derivative matters.", "No outcomes after the filing date are available, including rulings on the Benavides post-trial motion or the Ninth Circuit appeal.", "The filings do not rank the proceedings by severity, so no ranking is given."], "confidence": "medium", "confidence_reason": "The FY2025 10-K chunks cover most of the legal proceedings note, but some portions of Note 13 are missing from the retrieved context.", "next_questions": ["What is the status of the litigation over Elon Musk's 2018 compensation package?", "How did the Benavides verdict change between the Q3 FY2025 10-Q and the FY2025 10-K?", "What government investigations does Tesla disclose?", "Which legal proceedings did Tesla disclose under Item 103 of Regulation S-K?"], "refusal": null}, "citations_resolved": [{"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000", "claim": 